  "caption": "Quinn's first physio visit: nerves high, bag packed for every scenario, and skinny jeans for a knee problem.\n\nHere's what usually happens. First, a chat about what happened, what makes it better or worse, and your goals. Then a look at how you move, with some strength and range tests. Next, a plain-language explanation, some treatment and a plan for home.\n\nA few tips: wear shorts or a singlet so the area is easy to reach, bring any scans, reports and a medication list, ask your questions, and allow extra time because first visits run longer. You can say stop at any point.\n\nMajor injuries, chest pain or worsening numbness or weakness need medical care first.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
